---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl, useTranslations } from '../../../../i18n/utils';

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`SuperFont Privacy Policy - ${t('site.title')}`}
  description="What SuperFont collects, why, where your font files stay, how long data is kept, and what you can ask us to do with it."
  lang={lang}
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl w-full mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-36">
    <div class="text-center mb-16 md:mb-20">
      <span class="block text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-primary mb-3">SuperFont</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-text tracking-tight mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-sub">Effective Date: September 18, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none
      prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:tracking-tight
      prose-h2:text-xl prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:mb-4
      prose-p:text-text-sub prose-p:leading-7
      prose-li:text-text-sub
      prose-strong:text-text prose-strong:font-medium
      prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline
      prose-table:text-sm prose-th:text-text prose-td:text-text-sub
      prose-code:before:content-none prose-code:after:content-none
    ">
      <p>
        <strong>SuperFont</strong> ("the app") does not collect the font files you import.
        Your fonts and the configuration profiles built from them are handled entirely on your device.
        The app automatically collects only the minimum needed to fix errors and improve the app,
        and this policy explains exactly what that is.
      </p>
      <p>
        This policy applies Hyewon &amp; Insong's <a href="/en/privacy/">general privacy policy</a> to SuperFont specifically.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Font Files and Profiles</h2>
      <p>
        Font files you import from the Files app or iCloud Drive (TTF, OTF, TTC, WOFF, WOFF2, ZIP)
        <strong>are stored only in the app's storage on your device.</strong>
        The app never sends them to a server, and the developer cannot see them. There is no cloud sync.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>To install fonts, the app builds a configuration profile (<code>.mobileconfig</code>) on the device and hands it to Safari on the same device, which passes it to Settings.
          This happens over an on-device connection only (<code>127.0.0.1</code>); the profile and font data never leave the device.</li>
        <li>Copies the app keeps for reinstalling are deleted together with the app.</li>
        <li>Fonts installed through Settings are managed by iOS. They remain after the app is deleted, and disappear when you remove their profile under Settings &gt; General &gt; VPN &amp; Device Management.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Google Fonts Tab</h2>
      <p>
        When you open the Google Fonts tab, the app fetches the font catalog from Google's Web Fonts API (<code>googleapis.com</code>)
        and downloads the font files you pick from Google's servers. These requests happen <strong>only when you use that tab</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>The app includes no account information and nothing that identifies you in these requests.</li>
        <li>As with any internet request, Google receives request metadata such as your IP address.
          This is covered by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        <li>Downloaded font files stay on your device as described in section 1.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Information Collected Automatically</h2>
      <p>The following is collected to fix errors and improve the app.</p>

      <h3>Firebase Analytics (Google LLC)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Device information</strong>: device model, operating system version, language and region settings</li>
        <li><strong>App usage events</strong>: progress through the install wizard, the number and extensions of imported files, profile creation and deletion, and similar interactions</li>
        <li><strong>App version and build number</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Firebase installation ID</strong>: an anonymous identifier used to tell devices apart. It is not linked to your name, email, or any identity.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Usage events <strong>never include font names, file names, profile names, or URLs.</strong>
        Only aggregate values such as counts, extensions, step names, and device type are sent.
      </p>

      <h3>Firebase Crashlytics (Google LLC)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Stack traces from crashes</li>
        <li>Device model and operating system version</li>
        <li>App version and build number</li>
        <li>If a font file cannot be read or a profile cannot be built, the <strong>error type and the step where it happened</strong>.
          Error message text and file names are not included.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>The app does not collect names, email addresses, phone numbers, contacts, location, or photos.</p>

      <h2>4. Tracking and Advertising Identifiers</h2>
      <p>
        The app <strong>does not collect the advertising identifier (IDFA) and does not track you.</strong>
        It does not include the frameworks that handle advertising identifiers (AppTrackingTransparency, AdSupport),
        and therefore never asks for App Tracking Transparency permission. The app contains no advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        The App Store privacy label reads as follows, matching the privacy manifest shipped inside the app.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Linked to you</th><th>Used to track</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Identifiers — Device ID</td><td>Analytics</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Usage Data — Product Interaction</td><td>Analytics</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diagnostics — Crash Data</td><td>App Functionality</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diagnostics — Other Diagnostic Data</td><td>App Functionality</td><td>No</td><td>No</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>5. Why It Is Collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Diagnosing crashes and errors, and fixing bugs</li>
        <li>Improving the install wizard and other features, and the overall experience</li>
        <li>Understanding how the app is used, in aggregate</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Collected information is not used for any other purpose. If that ever changes, this policy will be revised and announced first.</p>

      <h2>6. Third Parties and Processors</h2>
      <p>The app relies on the following third parties.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Third party</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Google LLC (Firebase)</td><td>App analytics, crash reporting</td><td>Per the processor's policy</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Google LLC (Google Fonts)</td><td>Font catalog lookup and font file download, only when you request it</td><td>Per Google's policy</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>The developer never sells collected data or shares it beyond the purposes above.</p>

      <h2>7. Retention Period</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Firebase Analytics data</strong>: automatically deleted after at most 14 months</li>
        <li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics data</strong>: crash reports kept for at most 90 days</li>
        <li><strong>Font file copies</strong>: kept only on your device until you delete them in the app or delete the app</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Data past its retention period is destroyed without delay.</p>

      <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Opting out of tracking</strong>: the app does not track you and does not collect an advertising identifier, so no opt-out step is needed.</li>
        <li><strong>Stopping collection</strong>: deleting the app stops all further analytics and crash collection. There is no in-app switch to turn collection off separately.</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion requests</strong>: contact us at the address below to request deletion of collected data. Deletion within Firebase is handled within the limits of Firebase's own policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The app is not directed at children under 14 and does not knowingly collect their personal information.
        If we learn that such information has been collected, we delete it immediately.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Developer</strong>: Hyewon &amp; Insong</li>
        <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href="mailto:contact@hyewoninsong.com">contact@hyewoninsong.com</a></li>
        <li><strong>Response time</strong>: within 7 business days</li>
      </ul>
      <p>For help with installation, see the <a href="/en/apps/superfont/support/">SuperFont support page</a>.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be revised as laws or the app change.
        Any revision will be announced on this page at least 7 days before it takes effect.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 text-center">
      <a href="/en/apps/superfont/" class="text-sm font-medium text-primary hover:underline">← SuperFont</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
